Zero-force contact for DFT pens, and a pressure floor while in contact

The Slim Pen 2 on the Surface Pro 9 reports force like a switch: no pressure tone at all until
the tip is pressed, so small, light handwriting loses strokes. The tip signal itself tells
whether the pen is on the glass: its interpolated peak energy, relative to the level the same pen
has in frames where it reports force, is 0.85..1.0 with the pen resting on the glass without
force and below 0.3 at 5 mm (measured on the device). With ZeroForceContact the pen counts as in
contact at or above ZeroForceEnter of that reference and until it falls below ZeroForceExit; the
reference is learned from frames with force (or given with ZeroForceReference). ContactMinPressure
is the pressure reported while there is contact without force. Everything defaults to off.

